# The pinch point: the dimension of spacetime's algebra is forced to be exactly eight, squeezed from above and below, and
# the octonions are what sits there. This file checks the two arithmetic pressures by native evaluation. The CEILING:
# the Cayley-Dickson tower doubles dimension (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) and the norm survives only while the input is associative
# (Hurwitz), so composition algebras exist only at 1, 2, 4, 8 and die at 16 (the sedenions have zero divisors) -- the
# dimension is at most eight. The FLOOR: one substance means the directions you move (the vector, n components) and the
# matter that moves (the spinor, 2^(n/2-1) components) are the same size, which happens only at n = 8, since 2^3 = 8 -- the
# dimension is at least eight. At most eight and at least eight forces exactly eight.

# ---- THE CEILING: Cayley-Dickson doubling, composition stops at eight ----

# Each rung doubles the dimension: 1 -> 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16.
hold cayley-dickson-doubles-one-to-two
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 1

hold cayley-dickson-doubles-four-to-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 4

hold cayley-dickson-doubles-eight-to-sixteen
  call is-equal
    code 16
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 8

# The four composition-algebra dimensions are 1, 2, 4, 8: the reals, complexes, quaternions, octonions. Their product is
# 64 and their sum is 15, the fingerprint of exactly these four and no fifth (the would-be sixteen is excluded).
hold composition-dimensions-product
  call is-equal
    code 64
    call multiply
      code 1
      call multiply
        code 2
        call multiply
          code 4
          code 8

# ---- THE FLOOR: vector equals spinor only at eight ----

# At dimension eight the spinor has 2^(8/2 - 1) = 2^3 = 8 components, EQUAL to the vector's eight. One substance is
# satisfied: direction and matter are the same size.
hold vector-equals-spinor-at-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        code 2

# The CONTROL at dimension ten: the spinor has 2^(10/2 - 1) = 2^4 = 16 components, NOT equal to the vector's ten. One
# substance fails; the spinor has already raced ahead. This is why the floor is exactly eight and not higher.
hold spinor-overshoots-vector-at-ten
  call is-equal
    code 16
    call multiply
      code 2
      call multiply
        code 2
        call multiply
          code 2
          code 2

hold vector-ten-is-below-spinor-sixteen
  call is-below
    code 10
    code 16

# ---- THE PINCH: at most eight and at least eight ----

# The ceiling caps the dimension at eight (composition's top rung) and the floor lifts it to eight (vector = spinor), so
# the dimension is caught at exactly eight, where the composition algebra is the octonions. The two bounds meet: 8 = 8.
hold ceiling-meets-floor-at-eight
  call is-equal
    code 8
    code 8

# Spacetime is the rank of D4, half of eight: 8 / 2 = 4. One ordered time direction and three space.
hold spacetime-dimension-is-four
  call is-equal
    code 8
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 4
